# .cursorrules — Resume Craft

> Cursor AI assistant rules for Resume Craft project.

## Project Context

Resume Craft is a Next.js 15 App Router application — an AI-powered resume builder.

## Always Do

- Use `@/*` path aliases (resolves to `./src/*`)
- Use Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes for styling
- Use `cn()` from `@/shared/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- Use Zustand store (with Immer) for resume state mutations
- Use React Query for server-state (queries/mutations calling server actions)
- Use server actions (`"use server"`) for all backend logic — no API routes
- Use `getUniqId()` for generating UUIDs (uuid v7)
- Return `{ success, message, data?, error? }` from server actions
- Call `connectDb()` and `verifyAuth()` in authenticated server actions
- Import from feature barrel files (`@/features/documents`)
- Use `dynamic(() => ..., { ssr: false })` for PDF-rendering components

## Never Do

- Use browser DOM APIs (`<img>`, `<div>`) in @react-pdf/renderer templates
- Create API routes — use server actions only
- Modify shadcn/ui base components unless adding variants
- Import internal feature paths across feature boundaries
- Use inline styles in React components (except in PDF templates)
- Store secrets in code — use environment variables

## Tech Stack Quick Ref

- Next.js 15 (App Router, Turbopack, React Compiler)
- TypeScript strict
- Tailwind CSS v4 (oklch tokens)
- shadcn/ui (new-york) + Radix UI
- Zustand + Immer
- TanStack React Query v5
- Clerk auth
- MongoDB + Mongoose
- @react-pdf/renderer
- TipTap editor
- Groq SDK (AI)
- Motion (animations)
- PostHog (analytics)
- pnpm

## File Structure Convention

```
src/app/           → Pages & layouts (App Router)
src/backend/       → Server actions, DB models, config
src/features/      → Feature modules (self-contained)
src/shared/        → Cross-feature code (components, hooks, lib, types)
```
